 point='<b>The first word is "universe".</b> The thousand names open not with a god in a temple but with <i>viśvam</i>: everything. Then <i>viṣṇuḥ</i>, "the one who pervades it". The rest of this verse traces His relation to every being: He makes, holds, nourishes and is the Self of each.',
