 point='<b>Many-headed.</b> <i>Bahuśirāḥ</i> recalls the Puruṣa Sūkta: "the Person has a thousand heads, a thousand eyes, a thousand feet". The Lord sees, thinks and acts through every being. <i>Rudra</i> again carries two readings, as Śiva did in verse 4.',
